---
title: "Column Tooltips"
---

Column tooltips are set on the column definition and show for cells and column headers.

## Cell Tooltips

Set `tooltip: true` to have a tooltip match the value displayed in the cell whatever its source: a [Value Getter](./value-getters/), [Aggregation](./aggregation/) or a [Calculated Column](./calculated-columns/). A string value shows fixed text, and a callback enables generating the content dynamically from the cell value, `valueFormatted` or row data.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'athlete', tooltip: true },
        { field: 'country', tooltip: 'The country the athlete represents' },
        { field: 'year', tooltip: ({ value }) => `Games held in ${value}` },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Cell Tooltips" name="cell-tooltips" /%}

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["tooltip"] /%}

{% expandingSection headerText="TooltipCallbackParams" %}
{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="TooltipCallbackParams" /%}
{% /expandingSection %}

`tooltip: false` does not remove tooltips registered at runtime with [`setTooltip`](#tooltips-for-custom-components), or grid-owned validation and formula error tooltips.

## Header Tooltips

Use `headerTooltip: true` to show the displayed header name as the tooltip. A string shows fixed text instead, and a callback generates the content dynamically, receiving the header name as `value`. Column groups accept `headerTooltip` too.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'athlete', headerTooltip: "The athlete's full name" },
        { field: 'country', headerTooltip: true },
        { field: 'sport', headerTooltip: ({ value }) => `Column: ${value}` },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Header Tooltips" name="header-tooltips" /%}

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="header" names=["headerTooltip"] /%}

{% expandingSection headerText="HeaderTooltipCallbackParams" %}
{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="HeaderTooltipCallbackParams" /%}
{% /expandingSection %}

## Blank Values

Tooltips are not shown for the missing values `undefined`, `null` and `''` (empty string). To display a tooltip for a missing value, use a callback that returns non-empty content.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Blank Values" name="blank-values" /%}

## Tooltips for Truncated Text

Set `tooltipShowMode: 'whenTruncated'` to show tooltips only when the hovered or focused text is truncated. Built-in control tooltips do not require truncated text, except floating-filter value previews, which show only when truncated.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    tooltipShowMode: 'whenTruncated',
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltips" name="tooltip-show-mode" /%}

{% note %}
`tooltipShowMode = 'whenTruncated'` has no effect when using Browser Tooltips, as Browser Tooltips are controlled by the browser and not the grid.
{% /note %}

## Tooltips for Custom Components

Custom cell renderers and header components can register tooltip content at runtime with the `setTooltip` method on their params. `tooltip: false` and `headerTooltip: false` do not disable these. See [Cell Components](./component-cell-renderer/#tooltips), [Header Components](./column-headers-components/#tooltips) and [Column Groups](./column-groups/#tooltips).

## Row Groups

When a column is grouped, the generated group column inherits its tooltip configuration from the underlying column. Cell tooltip properties set on `autoGroupColumnDef` apply to leaf rows only; `headerTooltip` still applies to the group column header.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        {
            field: 'country',
            rowGroup: true,
            // inherited by group rows in the group column
            tooltip: ({ value }) => `Country: ${value}`,
        },
        { field: 'athlete' },
    ],
    autoGroupColumnDef: {
        // applies to leaf rows only; group rows inherit from their colDef
        tooltip: ({ data }) => `Athlete: ${data?.athlete}`,
    },
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Group Tooltip" name="rowgroups-tooltip" /%}

### Grouped Column Headers

With `groupDisplayType: 'multipleColumns'`, each generated group column header inherits the `headerTooltip` from its underlying column `colDef`.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    groupDisplayType: 'multipleColumns',
    columnDefs: [
        {
            field: 'country',
            rowGroup: true,
            // inherited by the generated group column header
            headerTooltip: 'Group by Country',
        },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Grouped Column Header Tooltip" name="rowgroups-header-tooltip" /%}

### Full Width Group Rows

With `groupDisplayType: 'groupRows'`, full-width group rows inherit their tooltips from the underlying column `colDef`.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Full Width Group Row Tooltip" name="rowgroups-fullwidth-tooltip" /%}

### Aggregated Cells

When a group row displays an aggregated value in a data column, hovering that cell shows a tooltip for the aggregated value, not the underlying row data.
